      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-02-14_WidnesExaminer_art0028" n="art0028">
        <head>Death of Sir Herbert Croft.</head>
        <p>Death of Sir Herbert Croft.</p>
        <p>Sir Herbert Croft, ninth baronet, died at Lugwar dine Court, Hereford, on Tuesday morning, at%er long illness of heart affection. Re was 63 years o age. He was deputy—chairman of Herefordshire Quarter Sessions, chairman. of Hereford County Petty Sessilnal Division, and had been H. H, In- spector of Constabulary since 1892, tie was formerly revising barrister of Shropshire, and Par- liamentary member for Herefordshire from 1858 to 1874. He is succeeded by his eldest sem, Mr Herbert Croft, formerly lieutenant in the Shropshire Light Infantry. Sir Herbert, in connection with his duty as inspector of constabulary, has paid many visits to Warrington. and was well known to tne members of the Watch Committee and the police force.</p>
      </div>
