        <p>ihe third day's play in this tournament commenced on Saturday, at the Ca-operation Hall, Hamerton-vtreet, Burnley. rhere was again a Itrge attendance, and in- cluded C W Holt (Hurt), T Townsend (Littleborough). PI Evans (fary), F Hartley (Nelson), ,J M Weir (d,,,„ cheater), W 11 Waller Ofilnibire), J Graham (Padiham), and other leading " lights." The unfiaished beat in the second rnund between Roberts (Warrongtoi ) and Hynd, 51.13. (Salford,) resulted in an!easy victory for the Warrington player, who won the first three game, played. The ballot for the third round produced entno good play, but the centre of attraction was un- doubtedly the board where &amp;Vie, of Darwen, and Blakelsy of Manclrster, faced each other. Th,ir first game, a " Belso," resulted in a (raw, but the next game, a "Single Corner," ought to have been woo by Lilakeley, who missed a c-mparativels. easy win. Their third game had to be adilurned at the following ro.4i- tion Black men on 3 and 22, kings on 19 and 23 ; White men on 12 and 28. kings on 10 and 20, White (Settle) to play. J Flynd, jun,and WClegg, played three fine games, the Bolton player having much the worst of matters. Some good play was exhibited in the other beats. Scores : Wins 0</p>
